00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Saints and Soldiers is a 2003 war drama film directed by Ryan
Little and produced by Little and Adam Abel.

12
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
It is loosely based on events that took place after the
Malmedy massacre during the Battle of the Bulge.

13
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:51,000
The film stars Corbin Allred, Alexander Niver, Lawrence Bagby, and Peter Asle Holden as four American
soldiers trying to return a British airman with vital intelligence to the Allied lines.

14
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
After researching World War II and the Battle of the Bulge,
Little began shooting in January 2003 in Utah.

15
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
Filming lasted 30 days.

16
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Little and Abel were able to save money on production by recruiting a group of World
War II reenactors who volunteered their services, costumes, and props.

17
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:51,000
Excel Entertainment released the film at festivals to garner
publicity before it was released to the public.

18
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
The movie won numerous Best Picture awards from over 15 film festivals.

19
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Critical reception was generally positive with praise towards the message, story, performances
(particularly of Allred and Niver), production values, and action sequences.

20
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Though the screenplay, pacing, and ties to Mormonism were criticized by some reviewers, several film scholars
argued that despite the Latter Day Saint (LDS)-related themes, the film appeals to a wide audience.

21
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
The movie's success launched its titular film series,
including three standalone sequels.

22
